      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Form 990, Part VI, Section B, Line 11b</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>THE FORM 990 IS REVIEWED BY THE CHIEF EXECUTIVE OFFICER AND FRACTIONAL CFO AND EMAILED TO ALL MEMBERS OF THE BOARD OF DIRECTORS PRIOR TO FILING.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Form 990, Part VI, Section B, Line 12c</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>THE IPS BOARD OF DIRECTORS OFFICER, DIRECTOR OR COMMITTEE MEMBER HAS A DUTY TO DISCLOSE ANY ACTUAL OR POSSIBLE FINANCIAL OR NONFINANCIAL CONFLICTS OF INTERSTEST TO THE BOARD OR EXECUTIVE COMMITTEE. SUCH DISCLOSURE WILL OCCUR ANNUALLY THROUGH THE COMPLETION OF THE ANNUAL STATEMENT. THE EXECUTIVE COMMITTEE OF THE BOARD OF DIRECTORS WILL REVIEW ALL DIRECTORS ANNUAL STATEMENT TO DETERMINE WHETHER ANY FINANCIAL OR NONFINANCIAL CONFLICTS OF INTEREST EXIST.IF IT IS DETERMINED THAT A FINANCIAL OR NONFINANCIAL CONFLICT OF INTEREST EXISTS, THE DIRECTOR WILL BE EXCLUDED FROM ANY DECISION OR DISCUSSION IN WHICH THE DIRECTORHAS A CONFLICT. ANY DIRECTOR MAY RECUSE HIMSELF OR HERSELF AT ANY TIME FROM INVOLVEMENT IN ANY DECISION OR DISCUSSION IN WHICH THE DIRECTOR BELIEVES HE OR SHE HAS OR MAY HAVE A CONFLICT OF INTEREST, WITHOUT GOING THROUGH THE PROCESS FOR DETERMINING WHETHER A CONFLICT OF INTEREST EXISTS.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Form 990, Part VI, Section B, Line 15a</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>A COMPREHENSIVE SALARY STUDY WAS COMPLETED BY A CONSULTANT AND USED TO INFORM THE BOARD OF REASONABLE COMPENSATION. THE CHIEF EXECUTIVE OFFICER'S COMPENSATIONARRANGEMENTS ARE APPROVED IN ADVANCE BY THE BOARD OF DIRECTORS AND ARE BASED UPON APPROPRIATE COMPARABILITY DATA FOR NON-PROFIT ORGANIZATIONS IN THE SOUTHERNCALIFORNIA REGION.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Form 990, Part VI, Section B, Line 15b</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>CEO &amp; TOP MANAGEMENT A COMPREHENSIVE SALARY STUDY WAS COMPLETED BY A CONSULTANT AND USED TO INFORM THE CHIEF EXECUTIVE OFFICER' WHO REVIEWS ALL KEY EMPLOYEE SALARIES. SALARIES ARE BASED UPON APPROPRIATE COMPARABILITY DATA FOR NON-PROFIT ORGANIZATIONS IN THE SOUTHERN CALIFORNIA REGION.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Form 990, Part VI, Section C, Line 19</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>Bylaws are available to the public; conflict of interest policy is an internal policy; financial statements and 990 are available upon request.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
